# The coefficients of the product of two polynomials of coefficients of one limb (milestone2.md,
# "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": conv_k): coefficient j of z, of n_x + n_y - 1 (none when a
# polynomial is empty), is the fused dot product dot_1, in its sequential order, of the terms
# (x_i, y_(j-i)), i from max(0, j - n_y + 1) to min(j, n_x - 1) in increasing order: each
# coefficient that is finite satisfies the statement of dot_1 for its own m_j terms,
# m_j <= min(n_x, n_y). A convolution (architecture.md, "Convolutions"), with the mask and the second
# pass of a map; the array written overlaps neither x nor y. Its arrays are stored, written through
# Kairn (the centers of bv_conv_1): kairn::conv of one limb calls conv_1_entry, whose coefficients
# guard their factors (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation).
fold:          conv_1
arrays:        stored x, stored y
coefficients:  dot_1
state:         mask finite
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential
writes:        z
check:         fold_finish_1
finish:        none
value:         x*y
ensures:       coefficients z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeFoldConv.v
terms_theorem: proofs/theories/FoldConv.v
status:        proved
domain:        extended
source:        dot_1 on the terms of each coefficient
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
